WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.520
A tragedy no child should bear.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.140
Ten children from the same family were on
their way to school when they spotted an exploded

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.470
bomb on the ground, a common sight in Afghanistan.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.620
They picked it up.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.710
The deadly device went off.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.710
Three children were killed.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:26.539
Seven survived, but they lost at least one
limb each.

00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:36.860
More than a year later they are struggling
to adapt.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.630
The day when the blast took place, it was
a bad day.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:50.290
I saw my brothers and sisters soaked in blood,
lying on the ground.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.329
My entire family was destroyed.

00:00:54.329 --> 00:01:03.490
The children are tutored at home, but sometimes
they have to go to school for exams.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:06.550
It's not an easy journey.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.710
Blisters form where the artificial limbs rub
their skin.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:13.219
A painful reminder of their new reality.

00:01:13.219 --> 00:01:21.780
When the explosion took place, I tried to
stand up and go home, but when I tried to

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.880
walk, I noticed that I didn't have my leg.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.049
This was a year ago, after the blast that
changed everything.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:37.030
Their story, a reminder of the war that still
rages on, even though the Taliban are in negotiations

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.189
with the US for some sort of peace settlement.

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:44.329
A resolution seems far off.

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:50.740
Decades of conflict have left the nation strewn
with landmines and other deadly devices.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:56.350
The UN says more than 900 children were killed
in 2018.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:01.459
Another 7000 were wounded.

00:02:01.459 --> 00:02:05.280
If peace comes, we will be very happy, there
will be no problem, everybody will be doing

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.140
their business without any tension, even if
we have disability at least we will have security

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.730
and peace.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:16.040
Everyday there is non-stop fighting and gunfire
and it has made our life terrible.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.980
The Afghan government and the Taliban must
sit together and agree on peace, so other

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:29.780
children do not get killed or get disabled
in this war.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:34.920
And though her childhood was taken away, Rabia
hopes that other children in Afghanistan can

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:40.140
still enjoy a normal childhood.

